# Antmicro's glTF models for the parts Jetson's board names through ${ANT3DMDL}, fetched from
# antmicro/hardware-components (Apache-2.0) at a fixed commit (PROVENANCE.md, "Antmicro's 3D models").
# `make remote` fetches them into remote/antmicro-models/hardware-components/, and the Makefile points
# AGNI_MODEL_VARS's ANT3DMDL there. agni reads a glTF beside each .step Jetson names (agni issue 1687).
#
# 48 of Jetson's 67 model names have a glTF here, covering 938 of its 1011 parts. 12 exist only as
# Blender files, and 7 not at all. Each glTF comes with the .bin it names. These are Antmicro's LOD2
# models, about a third of the full models' triangles, and each extent is within 0.04 mm of the full
# model's. agni draws them in its stack view (agni issue 1652) and takes heights from the same files.
#
# <sha256>  <folder>  <url at a fixed commit>
